# Accepted vulnerability risks for the Trivy image scan in .github/workflows/build-images.yml.
#
# The scan blocks a release on any CRITICAL vulnerability that has a fix available.
# Each entry needs a justification comment directly above it (CI checks this) and
# should carry an `exp:YYYY-MM-DD` date, after which Trivy stops ignoring it. Say
# what is affected, why the risk is acceptable for now, and who remediates it.
# Entries apply to every scanned image.
#
# No risks are accepted. The adoption baseline (perl-base, npm's bundled tar and
# esbuild's Go standard library in the product image) was fixed in product/Dockerfile.
